# A type this file declares, named like a pub function of a module the file
# imports. The file's own declaration should win (log, 2026-10-12, "a name
# the author declared wins over a builtin and an import"; 2026-10-18, "a
# module's own type beats an imported type's twin"). Should print
# `own_type_loses_to_imported_function/env "x" 0` on every engine when run
# with no arguments.
#
#   kanso play own_type_loses_to_imported_function.kso     the record, as above
#   kanso play own_type_loses_to_imported_function.kso --interp
#     <io> 0
#
# The interpreter builds `os/env "x"` instead, so the engines disagree.
# The same file with `type run` (three fields) and `run 1 2 3` is refused
# at check on every engine: `no 3-argument arm of `run` (arms take 2)`,
# because `run` resolves to `os/run`. Without `import "std/os"` both
# programs work, which is the case F1 of FRICTION.md was about.
import "std/os"

type env
  name

os/args .> (xs -> print "{env "x"} {length xs}")
